<title>NEW ZEALAND: Cultus abandons Skull Creek North 1 well.</title>
<headline>Cultus abandons Skull Creek North 1 well.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cultus Petroleum No Liability said on Tuesday it had plugged and abandoned the Skull Creek North 1 well in Australia's Otway Basin, with the rig released at 2300 hours on March 22.</p>
<p>It said DST 2b, testing the Cretaceous aged Eumeralla Formation over the interval 1515-1525 metres, flowed gas to surface at rate too small to measure through a 6.25 millimetre surface choke.</p>
<p>Cultus Petroleum is an oil and gas explorer. Its major shareholders are New Zealand bankers Michael Fay and David Richwhite, who own 30 percent of the issued capital.  </p>
<p>--Wellington Newsroom (64 4) 4734746</p>
